  "review": {
    "at_utc": "2026-11-21T04:41:00Z",
    "reviewer": "codex-primary-controller",
    "classification": "October UNSD workbook row 1931 and WCO HS 8908.00 expressly include whole vessels for breaking up. Withdrawal, sale, delivery and subsequent completion of recycling are separate events. Check actual intent and yard receipt, then exclude normal secondhand transfers, post-cut recovery, recovered individual materials and contracted services from the primary reference.",
    "primary_evidence": "The Maersk November 2016 owner publication records delivery and subsequent recycling of Wyoming and Georgia at Alang. Its original PDF was inspected, SHA-256 4bb7b8ec14ec3e04b6a3120d73c262817c87b1f3eca03a54462cecd02ef9fa45. The 2024 owner report records a separate set of completed recycling cases. Basel’s 2002 technical guidelines distinguish decommissioning/preparation from dismantling, PDF SHA-256 bc4589525c085d53fb8ce033561cf22ee25a71e8580a2f732811b1871bcef712. The Hong Kong Convention came into force in June 2025. The October 2026 BIMCO publication documents a sale and delivery framework, not its use for any particular historical vessel.",
    "measurement": "Reference M is the hull’s verified dry net mass at acceptance, excluding separately inventoried liquids and temporary loads. To use a recorded lightweight or statutory/contractual LDT requires a documented configuration bridge. Gross tonnage is not mass. Record actual physical fractions without adding a component again to whole-vessel mass. Track inherited service-to-retirement burdens by exchange and separate actual preparation or transport. Qualify or restrict results if the historical vector is absent. First reception alone creates Q, later services and returned lots retain original cohort identity. Distinguish first physical receipt without purchase, purchase and true return, and retain all real material crossings independent of supplier burden coverage.",
    "native_records": "The public yard-gate Waste with a CTUe reference is dimensionally unsuitable. Another genuine first-reception Waste uses Mass but is not the declared Product. A same-CPC generic manufactured Product/Mass cannot settle ship preparation and its specific release condition. Measurement Mass/kg and Energy units are independently archived. The pinned used-lubricant dataset is a Waste at generation and does not identify treatment. Preserve distinct air compartments, molecular species and fossil/biogenic carbon. No blanket relation to a fuel’s downstream treatment, a missing provider, or historic hull production is inferred.",
    "readiness": "Thirty-nine inventory cards per language. Ten native exchange identities bound and 29 unbound, including the whole vessel and several conditional interfaces. Independent pcr:check confirmed 390 checks performed, no skips and 39 warnings. Candidate/authored, Chinese aligned. Actual ship evidence, applicable agreements and authorities, species, yields, provider matching and independent scientific and formal translation review remain outstanding.",
